<title>USA: Illinois Central union approves contract.</title>
<headline>Illinois Central union approves contract.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-05-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Illinois Central Corp said Thursday 400 locomotive engineers at its Illinois Central Railroad ratified a wage contract reached last month.</p>
<p>Workers represented by the Brotherhood of Locomotive Engineers approved the contract, which settles wage and work-rule issues through 2000, the company said.</p>
<p>Illinois Central Railroad operates a 2,600-mile freight railroad between Chicago and the Gulf of Mexico.</p>
<p>	     -- Reuter Chicago Newsdesk 312-408-8787</p>
</text>
